# The monogamy of entanglement, read through the CHSH game. A pair of parties sharing a maximally entangled state can
# violate the Bell-CHSH inequality up to the Tsirelson bound, two times the square root of two, whose square is eight,
# well past the classical limit of two, whose square is four. But this strength cannot be shared. The Toner-Verstraete
# monogamy relation bounds the two CHSH values a single party can hold with two different partners: the sum of their
# squares cannot exceed eight. So if the first pair saturates the quantum maximum, its squared CHSH is eight, and the
# second pair is forced to squared value zero, no quantum correlation at all, only whatever a classical channel allows.
# This is the algebraic face of the wormhole being non-shareable: a maximal bridge to one partner leaves nothing for a
# third. Classical correlation escapes the bound differently: two classical values of two each give squared values four
# and four, summing to exactly eight, so classical correlation, unlike a quantum throat, can be shared both ways at once.
# This file checks the Tsirelson square, the quantum-beats-classical gap, and both faces of the monogamy sum reaching
# eight.

# The Tsirelson bound squared is eight: (2 root 2)^2 = 4 * 2 = 8, the quantum ceiling on a single CHSH value.
hold tsirelson-bound-squared-is-eight
  call is-equal
    code 8
    call multiply
      code 4
      code 2

# The classical CHSH bound is two, squared four, and quantum strictly exceeds it: 4 below 8.
hold quantum-tsirelson-beats-classical
  call is-below
    code 4
    code 8

# Monogamy at the singlet corner: the first pair takes the full squared strength eight, forcing the second pair to zero,
# 8 + 0 = 8, a maximal bridge to one partner and none to a third.
hold maximal-bridge-forbids-a-third
  call is-equal
    code 8
    call add
      code 8
      code 0

# Classical sharing fills the same monogamy budget symmetrically: two classical values of squared strength four each,
# 4 + 4 = 8, so a classical correlation can be held with both partners at once while a quantum throat cannot.
hold classical-correlation-shares-both-ways
  call is-equal
    code 8
    call add
      code 4
      code 4
